.TH PHP 1 "2026-07-19" "phplang 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
php \- compiled PHP runtime on the fusevm bytecode VM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIFILE\fR]
[\fIARGV\fR...]
.br
.B php
\-r \fICODE\fR
.br
.B php
\-a
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phplang
runs PHP programs by lexing and parsing to an AST, lowering to
.B fusevm
bytecode, and executing on the fusevm bytecode VM with a tracing Cranelift
JIT for hot arithmetic loops. There is no bespoke PHP VM or JIT; execution
and codegen live entirely in fusevm. PHP object semantics (arrays, strings,
type coercion) are served by a runtime host on top of the VM.
.PP
Source files use the standard \(oq\fI<?php ... ?>\fR\(cq and
\(oq\fI<?= ... ?>\fR\(cq tags; any text outside a PHP tag is passed through
verbatim as inline HTML.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-run " " \fICODE\fR
Run PHP code given directly on the command line, e.g.
\(oq\fIphp \-r 'echo 1+1;'\fR\(cq. The code is run as if wrapped in
\fI<?php ... ?>\fR; no opening tag is required.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-interactive
Start the interactive REPL. Also entered automatically when
.B php
is run with no
.I FILE
and stdin is a TTY.
.TP
.B \-\-tiers
Run it, then report which fusevm execution tier took each of its chunks.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-bytecode
Print the compiled fusevm bytecode for
.I FILE
(the main chunk and every user function's chunk) and exit, instead of
running it.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I FILE
The
.B .php
script to run. Omit to use
.B \-a
or
.BR \-r ,
or to read the script from stdin (non-interactive stdin with no
.I FILE
runs stdin as a script).
.TP
.I ARGV
Trailing arguments passed through to the running PHP program as
.BR $argv .
.SH LANGUAGE
Supported: scalars, variables and \fI$var\fR string interpolation, arithmetic
(\fI+ \- * / % **\fR), string concatenation (\fI.\fR), compound assignment,
increment/decrement (\fI++/\-\-\fR), loose and strict comparison
(\fI== != === !== < > <= >=\fR), logical operators (\fI&& || and or\fR), the
ternary operator (\fI?:\fR), indexed and associative arrays (literals, append
via \fI$a[]=\fR, index read/write), control flow (\fIif/elseif/else, while,
for, foreach, break, continue, return\fR), and user-defined functions with
positional parameters and recursion.
.PP
A standard library is built in, including string functions (\fIstrlen,
str_repeat, strrev, substr, strpos, str_replace, strtoupper, strtolower,
ucfirst, trim, ltrim, rtrim\fR), array functions (\fIcount, implode, explode,
in_array, array_keys, array_values, array_push, range\fR), math functions
(\fIabs, floor, ceil, round, sqrt, max, min, intval, floatval\fR), type
introspection (\fIgettype, is_array, is_int, is_float, is_string, is_bool,
is_null, is_numeric\fR), and output formatting (\fIsprintf, printf, print_r,
var_dump\fR), and more.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. 255 on a parse error or a fatal error, which are reported the way
the PHP CLI reports them: the display copy on stdout (\fIParse error: ...\fR /
\fIFatal error: Uncaught ...\fR with a stack trace) and a \fIPHP \fR-prefixed log
copy on stderr. 1 on a failure with no PHP equivalent, reported to stderr as
\fIphp: <reason>\fR and nothing else.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run a script:
.B php script.php
.TP
Run a one-liner:
.B php \-r 'echo 6 * 7;'
.TP
Start the REPL:
.B php \-a
.TP
Inspect the compiled bytecode:
.B php \-\-dump\-bytecode script.php
.SH SEE ALSO
Project: https://github.com/MenkeTechnologies/phplang
